            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="GRE04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Gregory</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1754">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1808"/>
                    <occupation>clergyman and writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Gregory seems a likely associate of Helen Maria Williams and her company. 
    Also in the 1787 list with <persName key="ROG01">S. Rogers</persName> and <persName key="WIL01">Helen Maria Williams</persName>.
    After <persName key="KIP01">Andrew Kippis's</persName> death Gregory became the editor of the <title>Biographia Britannica</title>.
    In that role he would have mixed with literary circles a good deal, and on this basis we have coded later entries in the 
    diary to Gregory as references to him until 1805. Many of the contacts are at <persName key="JOH01">Johnson's</persName>, 
    <persName key="PHI01">Phillips</persName>, or <persName key="ROB01">Robinson's</persName>. The entries that begin after 1816 are to another Gregory.
  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title/>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
